            "review_title": "Review at Kyung Bok Gung Korean Restaurant",
            "review_text": "SeattleEastsideRealEstate\nSeattle, Washington96 contributions\n0\nVery Good! Lots of side dishes - Tasted Quality\nNov 2019\nWe travel a lot and always try and eat Korean food at least 1 time in each location. we stumbled upon this gem which was a 5-10 minute walk from our Hotel (Park Hyatt). We way over ordered as we were so hungry but very happy with our selections. We ordered the seafood Pancake, Spicy pork, Short Beef Rib and Bean Paste Beef Soup. We would have been fine food quantity wise if we had omitted one of the items but we were very glad we got to taste it all. The side dishes (bon chon's) were plentiful. The Kim chee wasn't as ripe as I would have liked and I thought it odd I had to ask for a bowl of rice but maybe that's why every one is Vietnam is so skinny? :-) . Don't miss this Gem if you are looking for some different variety while visiting here. Our bill with a beer and food came to $65USD. A yummy experience that didn't break the bank. On a last note, we were surrounded by other Koreans so you know we were in the right place!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 16, 2019",
