            "review_text": "Tim W\nTaichung, Taiwan80 contributions\n1\nSpicy Korean Food and lots of bowing\nMay 2019 • Couples\nGet there early as it's very popular with Saigon Korean residents / tourists. Seems to be on about 5-6 floors, a veritable rabbit Warren of staff rushing about with plates of food. Vietnamese staff highly trained in Korean traditional manners. Lots of bowing and no small talk, and very attentive. The menu can be confusing unless you are conversant with Korean food, though plenty of pictures and part written in English. My companion ( Vietnamese) thought she had ordered 2 dishes, but I counted 21!!!! (Albeit small tasters) The food was healthy, fresh, varied and one had to adapt chopsticks handling skills to metal ones (more difficult). All in all a good meal at 550,000 dong which is reasonable for two. As we left, queuing already in the tight entrance foyer. Suitably replete, we stepped forth into the Saigon traffic and noise.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 29, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
